---
title: Gaviiformes
---
# Gaviiformes

Gaviiformes is a small order with a single living family, [[gaviidae]], holding
the five species of loon or diver. The legs are set so far back on the body that
walking on land is barely possible and the nest must be placed at the water's
edge. Bones are denser than in most flying birds, which lowers buoyancy and
makes the descent from the surface cheaper. The order has a long fossil record
and no close living relatives.
